-- Memory relations between places (proposal 050.1).
--
--   memory_alias(a, b)             a and b are one resource: a write through one is
--                                  read through the other.
--   memory_maybe_connected(a, b)   the memory of a and the memory of b may overlap.
--   memory_disconnected(a, b)      the memory of a and the memory of b do not overlap:
--                                  separation logic's a * b.
--
-- An operation states what a call of it leaves shared in its `ensures`:
-- `ensures memory_maybe_connected(result, l)` says where its result may live,
-- `ensures memory_alias(result, b)` that its result is `b` itself. It states what it
-- needs kept apart in its `requires`: `requires memory_disconnected(p, q)`. The typer
-- answers the relations inside an operation body, from what the body binds, builds and
-- calls; a rule body over the knowledge base answers nothing for them.
namespace anthill.memory
  rule memory_alias(?a, ?b)
  rule memory_maybe_connected(?a, ?b)
  rule memory_disconnected(?a, ?b) :- not(memory_maybe_connected(?a, ?b))
end
